<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dirty War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1976">1976</a>–<a href="/years/1983">1983</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Dirty War was the campaign of state terror waged by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a>'s military dictatorship between 1976 and 1983 against left-wing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrillas</a>, activists, students and other suspected opponents. Thousands were held in secret detention centres, tortured and killed, becoming the 'disappeared'; human rights groups estimate up to 30,000 victims. Leaders of the juntas were tried after democracy returned in 1983.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dirty-war.jpg" alt="Dirty War" width="320" height="358" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: U.S. Government · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jorge_Rafael_Videla_(2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
